<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul foreign exchange market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Seoul foreign exchange market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The foreign exchange market is closed in Seoul for Liberation Day, a public holiday. The market will reopen on Monday.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the won closed at 894.80, down from Wednesday's close of 894.30, after ranging from 894.30 to 895.00.</p>
<p>The won's mid-rate is expected to be pegged at 894.60 on Monday, compared with 894.30 on Thursday.</p>
</text>
